  "explanation": "The question asks when *St. John's Evangelical Lutheran Church* was built. Multiple distinct referents exist:\n\n1. **St. John's Evangelical Lutheran Church (Livingston, New York)**: D1S4 and D2S1 both state it was built in **1901-1902**.\n2. **St. John's Evangelical Lutheran Church (Springfield, Ohio)**: D4S4, D5S1, and D6S4 indicate the current large church building was constructed in the **1890s**.\n3. Another **St. John's Evangelical Lutheran Church** (Missouri): D7S6 states the current brick building was constructed in **1893**.\n\nThe answer **1850-1851** (from D3S1) refers to an unrelated or possibly misattributed version of the same name. Similarly, **October 1860** (D7S4) refers to the first wooden structure of a different church in Missouri, not the main building. These are not relevant to the primary construction of the named church in the question."
